  C3 C,                                                                                                                         DECIMAL                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                         ( FRACT-OV   [FRACTAL]                                 8-13-85) HEX V: [FRACTAL] -2 DP +! ( std xmid ymid x1 y1 x2 y2 rtn -- )    8B C, EC C, 8B C, 46 C, 04 C, 2B C, 46 C, 08 C, 48 C, 7E C,     05 C, B8 C, 01 C, 00 C, EB C, 02 C, 33 C, C0 C, 89 C, 06 C,     DX>1 ,  8B C, 4E C, 02 C, 2B C, 4E C, 06 C, 49 C, 7E C, 05 C,   B9 C, 01 C, 00 C, EB C, 02 C, 33 C, C9 C, 89 C, 0E C, DY>1 ,    0B C, C1 C, 7E C, 64 C, E8 C, MIDPT HERE 2+ - , E8 C, EDGES     HERE 2+ - ,  E8 C, CENTER HERE 2+ - ,  E8 C, NEWSTD HERE 2+ -   ,  33 C, C0 C, FF C, 76 C, 0E C, 50 C, 50 C, FF C, 76 C, 08 C,  FF C, 76 C, 06 C, FF C, 76 C, 0C C, FF C, 76 C, 0A C, E8 C,     [FRACTAL] HERE 2+ - , 33 C, C0 C, FF C, 76 C, 0E C, 50 C,       50 C, FF C, 76 C, 0C C, FF C, 76 C, 06 C, FF C, 76 C, 04 C,     FF C, 76 C, 0A C, E8 C, [FRACTAL] HERE 2+ - , 33 C, C0 C,       FF C, 76 C, 0E C, 50 C, 50 C, FF C, 76 C, 08 C, FF C, 76 C,     0A C, FF C, 76 C, 0C C, FF C, 76 C, 02 C, E8 C, [FRACTAL]       HERE 2+ - , 33 C, C0 C, FF C, 76 C, 0E C, 50 C, 50 C,         ( FRACT-OV   [FRACTAL] con't                           8-13-85) HEX                                                               FF C, 76 C, 0C C, FF C, 76 C, 0A C, FF C, 76 C, 04 C,           FF C, 76 C, 02 C, E8 C, [FRACTAL] HERE 2+ - ,  58 C, 83 C,      C4 C, 0E C, 8B C, EC C, 50 C, C3 C,                           DECIMAL                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                         ( FRACT-OV   FRACTALIZE  FILLARRAY                     8-13-85) HEX                                                             V: FRACTALIZE -2 DP +!                                            ( std 0 0 x1 y1 x2 y2 --) HERE DUP 2- !                         89 C, 2E C, RTEMP , E8 C, [FRACTAL] HERE 2+ - , 8B C,           2E C, RTEMP , AD C, 8B C, D8 C, FF C, 27 C,                                                                                   V: FILLARRAY -2 DP +! ( val -- \ fill current array with val)     HERE DUP 2- !  58 C, 8B C, 1E C, 'ARRAY , 8B C, 4F C, 04 C,     8B C, 5F C, 06 C, 06 C, 57 C, 8E C, C3 C, 33 C, FF C, F3 C,     AA C, 5F C, 07 C, AD C, 8B C, D8 C, FF C, 27 C,               DECIMAL                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                         ( FRACT-OV   FRACT-REGION                             11-19-84)                                                                 HEAD: FRACT-REGION ( -- \ do a fractal for)                       ( current region)                                             T:  STD @  0 0  XLL @  YLL @                                      XUR @ YUR @  FRACTALIZE T;                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    ( FRACT-OV   MERCATOR-GEN                              8-13-85)                                                                 : MERCATOR-GEN ( seed -- \ generate a)                            ( fractal mercator map given seed)                              DUP SEED !   GLOBALSEED !                                       XYANCHOR OFF                                                    MERCATOR-RATIO  MERCATOR-SCALE                                  SETSCALE                                                        SPHEREWRAP ON   SIGNEXTEND ON                                   ' MERCATOR SETLARRAY                                            0 0 48 23 SETREGION                                             FNULL FILLARRAY                                                 GENANCHORS                                                      SETANCHORS                                                      FRACT-REGION ;                                                                                                                ( FRACT-OV   CONTOUR-RATIO CONTOUR                    11-19-84) 20882 32767 2C: CONTOUR-RATIO                                             20 C: CONTOUR-SCALE  ( STD)                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                           ( FRACT-OV   INIT-CONTOUR                              8-13-85)                                                                 : INIT-CONTOUR ( -- \ initialize the)                             ( contour array to null.)                                       ' CONTOUR SETLARRAY                                             FNULL FILLARRAY ;                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                             ( FRACT-OV   MERC>CONANCHOR                            8-13-85)                                                                 HEAD: MERC>CONANCHOR ( -- \ populate )                            ( conachor from mercator array)                               T:    YCON @ 40 / Y2 !                                            XCON @ 48 / X2 !                                                SPHEREWRAP ON  ' MERCATOR SETLARRAY                             4 0 DO  ( 4 rows)                                               3 0 DO  ( 3 cols)                                                   I X2 @ +  Y2 @ J +  ACELLADDR A@                                I 4 *     J 2*      CONANCHOR LC!                               LOOP LOOP T;                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                              ( FRACT-OV   AV-MIDPT                                 11-19-84) HEAD: AV-MIDPT ( x1 y1 x2 y2 -- \ )                               ( find midpt and store average val)                           T:  2OVER ACELLADDR A@ >R ( -- n1)                                2DUP  ACELLADDR A@ R> + 2/ >R ( -- n')                          ROT + 2/ >R      ( x1 x2 -- y' n')                              + 2/ R> R>       ( x' y' n' --)                                 ROT ROT          ( n  x' y' --)                                 ACELLADDR A! T;                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                               ( FRACT-OV   CONANCHOR-HOR                            11-19-84) HEAD: CONANCHOR-HOR ( -- \ average )                              ( horizontals to fill in anchors)                             T:  4 0 DO                                                        2 0 DO                                                              I 4 * J 2* OVER 4 + OVER AV-MIDPT                               I 4 * J 2* OVER 2 + OVER AV-MIDPT                            I 1+ 4 * J 2* OVER 2 - OVER AV-MIDPT                               LOOP LOOP T;                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                              ( FRACT-OV   CONANCHOR-VER CONANCHOR-CNT1             11-19-84) HEAD: CONANCHOR-VER ( -- \ average )                              ( verticals to fill in anchors)                               T:  3 0 DO                                                        3 0 DO                                                              I 4 * J 2* OVER OVER 2+ AV-MIDPT                                LOOP LOOP T;                                                                                                              HEAD: CONANCHOR-CNT1 ( -- \ average )                             ( to fill center holes)                                       T:  3 0 DO                                                        2 0 DO                                                          I 4 * J 2* 1+ OVER 4 + OVER AV-MIDPT                                LOOP LOOP T;                                                                                                                                                                              ( FRACT-OV   CONANCHOR-CNT2                           11-19-84) HEAD: CONANCHOR-CNT2 ( -- \ average )                             ( to fill center holes)                                       T:  3 0 DO                                                        4 0 DO                                                              I 2* 1+ J 2* OVER OVER 2+ AV-MIDPT                              LOOP LOOP T;                                                                                                              HEAD: SETRELORIGIN                                              T:  YO' ! XO' ! T;                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                              ( FRACT-OV   CONANCHOR>CONTOUR                        11-19-84) head: dup. t: dup . t;                                          HEAD: CONANCHOR>CONTOUR ( -- \ move anchors)                      ( from conanchor to the contour array)                        T:  >0font cr XCON @ dup. 48 MOD 12 /                             YCON @ dup. 40 MOD 20 / ( x y --origin)                                            ( in conanchor)                              OVER XCON @ 48 / 48 * SWAP 12 * + >R                                 YCON @ 40 / 40 * OVER 20 * +                                    R> 2dup . . swap SETRELORIGIN                              6 0 DO  ( rows) cr                                              6 0 DO  ( cols)                                                     OVER I + OVER J + CONANCHOR LC@ dup.                            I 12 * J 20 * CONTOUR LC!                                       LOOP LOOP 2DROP   >1font T;                                                                                               ( FRACT-OV   ANCHOR-CONTOUR                           11-19-84) : ANCHOR-CONTOUR ( -- \ place anchors )                           ( for sub-contour regions within the)                           ( contour array based on the mercator)                          ( map and xcon,ycon, the ul corner of)                          ( the contour map)                                              MERC>CONANCHOR                                                  ' CONANCHOR SETLARRAY                                           CONANCHOR-HOR                                                   CONANCHOR-VER                                                   CONANCHOR-CNT1                                                  CONANCHOR-CNT2                                                  CONANCHOR>CONTOUR ;                                                                                                                                                                                                                                           ( FRACT-OV   SUB-CON-FRACT                             4-14-86) HEAD: SUB-CON-FRACT ( col row -- \ fractal)                       ( sub-contour region col,row if null)                         T:  20 * SWAP 12 * SWAP  ( x y --)                                OVER 1+ OVER 1+ ACELLADDR A@                                    FNULL = >R                       \                              OVER 11 + OVER 19 + ACELLADDR A@ \                              FNULL = R> AND                   \ check for null subregion     IF OVER 12 + OVER 20 + SETREGION                                   FRACT-REGION                                                 ELSE 2DROP THEN T;                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                            ( FRACT-OV   FRACT-CONTOUR                            11-19-84) : FRACT-CONTOUR ( -- \ fractalize all)                            ( sub-contour regions in the contour)                           ( map that contain nulls. Anchors are)                          ( assumed to be in place.)                                      SPHEREWRAP OFF  SIGNEXTEND ON                                   ' CONTOUR SETLARRAY                                             XYANCHOR ON                                                     CONTOUR-RATIO CONTOUR-SCALE                                     SETSCALE                                                        5 0 DO  ( for each row)                                         5 0 DO  ( for each col)                                             I J SUB-CON-FRACT                                               LOOP LOOP ;                                                                                                                                                                               ( FRACT-OV  +FRAME -FRAME @FRAME !FRAME                8-13-85) V: FRAME  ( stack frame pointer) HEX                            V: +FRAME -2 DP +! ( set stack frame) HERE DUP 2- !               89 C, 26 C, FRAME , AD C, 8B C, D8 C, FF C, 27 C,             V: -FRAME -2 DP +! ( drop stack frame) HERE DUP 2- !              83 C, C4 C, 0E C, 89 C, 26 C, FRAME , AD C, 8B C, D8 C,         FF C, 27 C,                                                   V: @FRAME -2 DP +!                                                            ( b -- n \ get word at [FRAME]+b) HERE DUP 2- !     5B C, 03 C, 1E C, FRAME , FF C, 37 C, AD C, 8B C, D8 C,         FF C, 27 C,                                                   V: !FRAME -2 DP +!                                                            ( n b -- \ store word at [FRAME]+b) HERE DUP 2- !   5B C, 03 C, 1E C, FRAME , 8F C, 07 C, AD C, 8B C, D8 C,         FF C, 27 C,                                                   DECIMAL                                                         ( FRACT-OV  @X1 @X2 @XMID @Y1 @Y2 @YMID !XMID !YMID... 8-13-85)                                                                 HEAD: @X1   T:   6 @FRAME T;                                    HEAD: @X2   T:   2 @FRAME T;                                    HEAD: @XMID T:  10 @FRAME T;                                    HEAD: @Y1   T:   4 @FRAME T;                                    HEAD: @Y2   T:   0 @FRAME T;                                    HEAD: @YMID T:   8 @FRAME T;                                    HEAD: @STD  T:  12 @FRAME T;                                    HEAD: !XMID T:  10 !FRAME T;                                    HEAD: !YMID T:   8 !FRAME T;                                    HEAD: !STD  T:  12 !FRAME T;                                                                                                    HEAD: MIDPTT ( -- \ compute midpoint for current frame)         T: @X1 @X2 + 2/ !XMID  @Y1 @Y2 + 2/ !YMID T;                                                                                    ( FRACT-OV - OUTPOLY                                 11-26-84 )                                                                 V= POLYPTR   V: POLYCOUNTER                                     V: ULY       V: ULX                                                                                                                                                                             HEAD: OUTPOLY ( -- \ save current polygon in the display list)  \ Build initial display list in main view buffer to guarantee   \ enough room.                                                  T:  POLYPTR @ >R   @STD HBUF-SEG @ I LC! ( surface byte)          @X1 ULX @ - HBUF-SEG @ I 1+   LC!                               ULY @ @Y1 - HBUF-SEG @ I 2+   LC! ( upper left corr)            @X2 ULX @ - HBUF-SEG @ I 3 +  LC!                               ULY @ @Y2 - HBUF-SEG @ R> 4 + LC! ( lower right cor)            5 POLYPTR +!   1 POLYCOUNTER +! T;                                                                                            ( FRACT-OV - ?HOMOGENOUS                          rfg03jun85)                                                                   HEAD: ?HOMOGENOUS                                                             ( -- t \ is currnt region all same surface type?) T:  @X1 @Y1 1- MERCATOR L+-@ COLORMAP                             COLOR @ !STD   ( get & save color)                              @Y1 @Y2 DO                                                        @X2 @X1 DO I J MERCATOR L+-@ COLORMAP color @ @STD = NOT                   IF 999 !STD LEAVE THEN ( end on 1st exception)               LOOP                                                            @STD 999 = IF LEAVE THEN                                      LOOP                                                    @STD 999 = NOT T;                                                                                                                                                                                                                                             ( FRACT-OV - POLYGON-EXTRACT                          8-13-85 )                                                                 : POLYGON-EXTRACT ( 0 0 0 X1 Y1 X2 Y2 -- )                        +FRAME                                ( set stack frame)        ?HOMOGENOUS                           ( is polygon solid?)      IF OUTPOLY                            ( if so, output poly)     ELSE MIDPTT                           ( else, subdivide...)        0 0 0 @X1 @Y1 @XMID @YMID MYSELF   ( &try again)                0 0 0 @XMID @Y1 @X2 @YMID MYSELF                                0 0 0 @X1 @YMID @XMID @Y2 MYSELF                                0 0 0 @XMID @YMID @X2 @Y2 MYSELF                             THEN                                                            -FRAME ;                   ( clear stack frame)                                                                                                                                                                                                               ( FRACT-OV - BUILD-CONTINENTS                         10-07-85)                                                                 HEAD: BUILD-CONTINENTS                                                             ( -- \ build polygon list for all faces)     T:  POLYPTR OFF                                                   72 0 DO 0 0 0                                                           I 12 /MOD  ( rem y --)                                          6 swap - 2* 2* DUP ULY ! SWAP                                   4 *  DUP ULX ! ( y x -- upper lft)                              SWAP OVER 4 + OVER 4 -  POLYCOUNTER OFF                         POLYPTR @ 0 I FACE L!                                           POLYGON-EXTRACT  POLYCOUNTER @ 2 I FACE LC!                  LOOP T;                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                  ( FRACT-OV - +TMP -TMP @TMP !TMP                      8-13-85 ) V: [TMP] ( temp variable base pointer) HEX                      V: +TMP -2 DP +! ( #cells -- \ reserve temp wkspace in stk)       HERE DUP 2- ! 89 C, 26 C, [TMP] , 58 C, D1 C, E0 C, 2B C,       E0 C, AD C, 8B C, D8 C, FF C, 27 C,                           V: -TMP -2 DP +! ( #cells -- \ reclaim temp wkspace in stk)       HERE DUP 2- ! 58 C, D1 C, E0 C, 03 C, E0 C, AD C, 8B C, D8 C,   FF C, 27 C,                                                   V: @TMP -2 DP +! ( cell# -- val \ @ val of temp cell#) HERE DUP   2- ! 5B C, D1 C, E3 C, F7 C, DB C, 03 C, 1E C, [TMP] , FF C,    37 C, AD C, 8B C, D8 C, FF C, 27 C,                           V: !TMP -2 DP +! ( val cell# -- \ save val in cell#) HERE DUP     2- ! 5B C, D1 C, E3 C, F7 C, DB C, 03 C, 1E C, [TMP] , 58 C,    89 C, 07 C, AD C, 8B C, D8 C, FF C, 27 C,                     DECIMAL                                                                                                                         ( FRACT-OV - CACCUM                                    8-13-85) V= FADDR       ( facet display list revision pointer)           V: MAINCOLOR   ( predominant color of face)                     V: TAD         ( temporary address holder)                      V: #POL        ( new polygon count)                             HEAD: CACCUM ( color -- \ accumulate occurances of color)       T:  32 0 DO DUP             ( color color -- \ preserve color)            I @TMP            ( get comparison color)                       DUP 0=            ( is comparison color missing?)               IF 2DROP I !TMP 1 I 1+ !TMP ( install new color)                   LEAVE                                                        ELSE =            ( matches comparison?)                           IF I 1+ DUP @TMP   1+ SWAP !TMP  LEAVE DROP THEN             THEN 2 +LOOP T;                                                                                                                                                                       ( FRACT-OV - MAJOR-COLOR                               8-13-85)                                                                 HEAD: MAJOR-COLOR                                                             ( addr count -- color \ find main color for face) T:  >R >R                                                         34 +TMP   [TMP] @ 68 - 70 0 FILL ( set aside temp workspace)    R> R> 0 DO HBUF-SEG @ OVER LC@ CACCUM  5 + LOOP DROP            32 0 DO I @TMP  I 1+ @TMP      ( color count --)                        DUP   33 @TMP          ( get current max count)                 > IF  33 !TMP  32 !TMP ( save new max)                            ELSE DROP 0= IF LEAVE THEN                                      THEN                                                    2 +LOOP                                                       32 @TMP >R   34 -TMP  R> T;                                                                                                                                                                   ( FRACT-OV - DROP-POLY PUSH-POLY POP-POLY              8-13-85) HEX                                                             V: DROP-POLY -2 DP +! ( [6 bytes] -- \ drop pgon from stk)        HERE DUP 2- ! 83 C, C4 C, 06 C, AD C, 8B C, D8 C, FF C,         27 C,                                                         V: PUSH-POLY -2 DP +! ( addr -- [6 bytes] \ push pgon onto stk)   HERE DUP 2- ! 8C C, C1 C, 8B C, 16 C, HBUF-SEG , 8E C,          C2 C, 33 C, C0 C, 5B C, 26 C, 8A C, 07 C, 43 C, 26 C,           FF C, 37 C, 83 C, C3 C, 02 C, 26 C, FF C, 37 C, 50 C,           8E C, C1 C, AD C, 8B C, D8 C, FF C, 27 C,                     V: POP-POLY -2 DP +! ( [6 bytes] -- \ pop polygon at FADDR)       HERE DUP 2- ! 8C C, C1 C, 8B C, 16 C, ' POLYSEG , 8E C,         C2 C, 8B C, 1E C, FADDR , 58 C, 26 C, 88 C, 07 C, 83 C,         C3 C, 03 C, 26 C, 8F C, 07 C, 83 C, EB C, 02 C, 26 C, 8F C,     07 C, 83 C, C3 C, 04 C, 89 C, 1E C, FADDR , 8E C, C1 C,         AD C, 8B C, D8 C, FF C, 27 C, DECIMAL                         ( FRACT-OV - ?MCLR MAINPOLY                            8-13-85) HEX                                                             V: ?MCLR -2 DP +!                                                            ( color-byte -- color-byte t \ main color?)          HERE DUP 2- !  33 C, C0 C, 58 C, 50 C, 3B C, 06 C, MAINCOLOR ,  75 C, 05 C, B8 C, 01 C, 00 C, EB C, 02 C, 33 C, C0 C, 50 C,     AD C, 8B C, D8 C, FF C, 27 C,                                 V: MAINPOLY -2 DP +!                                                        ( -- [4 4 0 0 color] \ build main polygon)            HERE DUP 2- !  33 C, C0 C, 50 C, B8 C, 04 C, 00 C, 8A C, E0 C,  50 C,  8B C, 06 C, MAINCOLOR , 50 C, AD C, 8B C, D8 C, FF C,    27 C,                                                         DECIMAL                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                         ( FRACT-OV - REDUCE-FACE                             11-26-84 )                                                                 HEAD: REDUCE-FACE ( face# -- \ remove redundant polygons)       T:  0 OVER FACE OVER OVER L@ TAD ! 2+ LC@ ( face# polygon-cnt- )  >R TAD @ I MAJOR-COLOR MAINCOLOR !    ( face# -- count)         I 0 DO TAD @ PUSH-POLY 5 TAD +! LOOP  ( face# -- count)         FADDR @ TAD !  MAINPOLY 1 #POL !  POP-POLY                      R> 0 DO ?MCLR IF DROP-POLY                                                    ELSE POP-POLY 1 #POL +!                                         THEN                                                   LOOP                                                       0 SWAP FACE OVER OVER TAD @ ROT ROT L!        ( addr --)        2+ #POL @ ROT ROT LC! T;                                                                                                                                                                                                                                      ( FRACT-OV - REDUCE-ALL MAKE-GLOBE                   11-26-84 )                                                                 HEAD: REDUCE-ALL                                                             ( -- \ reduce # of polygons & reclaim dictionary)  T:  0 FADDR !     ( set initial polygon list addr)                72 0 DO I REDUCE-FACE LOOP T;                                                                                                 : MAKE-GLOBE BUILD-CONTINENTS REDUCE-ALL ;                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                      ( FRACT-OV - UPSCRL DNSCRL                            12-17-84)                                                                 HEAD: UPSCRL ( n -- \ scroll current array up n rows )            ( { from row 0 to row n } )                                   T:  0 0 ACELLADDR         ( n sseg soff --)                       ROT 0 SWAP ACELLADDR  ( sseg soff dseg doff -- )                3 PICK OVER - ABS     ( sseg soff dseg doff #bytes-not-moved)   #BYTES SWAP -         ( sseg soff dseg doff count -- )          <LCMOVE T;                                                                                                                    HEAD: DNSCRL ( n -- \ scroll current array up n rows)           T:  0 SWAP ACELLADDR   ( sseg soff -- )                           0 0 ACELLADDR      ( sseg soff dseg doff -- )                   3 PICK OVER - ABS  ( sseg soff dseg doff #bytes-not-moved)      #BYTES SWAP -      ( sseg soff dseg doff count -- )             LCMOVE T;                                                     ( FRACT-OV - RTSCRL LFSCRL                            12-17-84)                                                                 HEAD: RTSCRL ( n -- \ scroll right current array n cols)        T:  #ROWZ 0 DO      ( for each row)                                       0 I ACELLADDR           ( n sseg soff --)                       3 PICK I ACELLADDR      ( n sseg soff dseg doff --)             #COLZ 6 PICK - <LCMOVE                                          LOOP DROP T;                                                                                                          HEAD: LFSCRL ( n -- \ scroll left current array n cols)         T:  #ROWZ 0 DO      ( for each row)                                       DUP I ACELLADDR         ( n sseg soff --)                       0   I ACELLADDR         ( n source dest -- )                    #COLZ 6 PICK - LCMOVE                                           LOOP DROP T;                                                                                                          ( FRACT-OV - SCRLXCON                                 12-17-84)                                                                 HEAD: SCRLXCON ( -- \ scroll the contour map left or right and)   ( null the area that is to be regenerated.)                   T:  DXCON @                                                       IF DXCON @ DUP 0<                                                  IF ABS RTSCRL 0 0 11 100                                        ELSE LFSCRL  49 0 60 100                                        THEN                                                            SETREGION FNULL FILLREGION                                   THEN T;                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                       ( FRACT-OV - SCRLYCON                                 12-17-84)                                                                 HEAD: SCRLYCON ( -- \ scroll the contour map up or down and)      ( null the area that is to be regenerated.)                   T:  DYCON @                                                       IF DYCON @ DUP 0<                                                  IF ABS UPSCRL  0  0 60 19                                       ELSE DNSCRL    0 81 60 100                                      THEN                                                            SETREGION FNULL FILLREGION                                   THEN T;                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                       ( FRACT-OV - SCRLCON                                  12-17-84)                                                                 : SCRLCON ( -- \ scroll the contour map to put the viewing )      ( frame back on the contour map.)                               DXCON @ DYCON @ OR                                              IF SPHEREWRAP OFF                                                  ' CONTOUR SETLARRAY                                             SCRLXCON ( scroll and null region)                              SCRLYCON ( scroll and null region)                              ANCHOR-CONTOUR                                                  FRACT-CONTOUR                                                THEN ;                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                        ( FRACT-OV ------ OVERLAY SUFFIX -----------------rfg03jun85)   trace @ trace off dispose trace !                               CLOSE-OVERLAY                                                   71 OVERLAY FRACT-OV                                             FRACT-OV                                                        FORTH DEFINITIONS                                               : MERCATOR-GEN ( seed -- ) FRACT-OV FRACT MERCATOR-GEN ;        : INIT-CONTOUR ( -- )      FRACT-OV FRACT INIT-CONTOUR ;        : ANCHOR-CONTOUR ( -- )    FRACT-OV FRACT ANCHOR-CONTOUR ;      : FRACT-CONTOUR ( -- )     FRACT-OV FRACT FRACT-CONTOUR ;       : MAKE-GLOBE ( -- )        FRACT-OV FRACT MAKE-GLOBE ;          : SCRLCON    ( -- )        FRACT-OV FRACT SCRLCON    ;                                                                          OV-CANCEL                                                       \ ' MERCATOR-GEN ' cM-GEN ! \ patch forward ref from shpmov-ov  \ cr ." cM-GEN is set to " cm-gen u.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                            